{100}{}{You see Hector.}
{101}{}{You see a Mexican man with long hair. He's dressed in a rough canvas shirt, a red bandana wrapped around his head.}
{102}{}{No hablo inglés.}
{103}{}{«I take it back. Looks like you can scrape by out here after all.»}
{104}{}{«Guess I misjudged the captain. Looks like you can scrape by out here after all.»}
{105}{}{«We're sailing back to our home port!»}

{200}{}{«Hey, amigo. You speak Spanish? Good. We need to talk.»}
{201}{}{«About what?»}
{202}{}{«Have you talked to Cesareo yet? He's trying to settle this bay. I say it's a lousy idea.»}
{1202}{}{«Have you talked to Cesareo yet? He's trying to settle this bay. I say it's a lousy idea.»}
{203}{}{«Why?»}
{204}{}{«We're cut off from civilization. Out here, you live or die on your own. And what do we have? One boat. A pile of scrap from the ruins. Inland it's nothing but dead mountains. There's NOTHING here! Even fishing means heading far out to sea - the coastline's poisoned.»}
{205}{}{«So what do you suggest?»}
{206}{}{«The captain's led us straight into hell! It's time to give him the black mark and head back to Mexico. I'm not the only one thinking it. Help us turn him around. Whatever he asks you to do - do the opposite. And if he still won't listen... then things get bloody. You understand?»}
{207}{}{«Alright. I'll keep it in mind.»}
{208}{}{«Damn... life's really chewed you up. Just don't tell me we'll end up the same way out here. You do speak Spanish, right? Good. We need to talk.»}

{210}{}{«No one's set foot here since the Apocalypse. We need to leave. Now.»}
{211}{}{«Maybe.»}
{212}{}{«The captain's led us astray! Time to give him the black mark.»}
{213}{}{«Your captain's dead. You're free to do whatever you want now.»}
{214}{}{«This is our chance! Time to get out of this cursed place. But there's one last problem - the schooner's water pump is busted. Without it, we won't make it far. She's docked at Fondeport.»}
{215}{}{«Alright. I'll see what I can do.»}
{216}{}{«The schooner's ready to sail.»}
{217}{}{«Cesareo's changed his mind. He's agreed to leave.»}
{218}{}{(grips your hand tightly) «Fate itself brought you to us. Goodbye, friend.»}
{1218}{}{(pulls you into a tight hug) «Fate itself brought you to us. Goodbye, friend.»}
{219}{}{«Fate itself brought you to us. Goodbye, friend.»}
{1219}{}{«Fate itself brought you to us. Goodbye, friend.»}
{220}{}{«Fair winds. Goodbye.»}
{221}{}{«So this is what this land does to people - strips them down to animals like you? That's bad. We need to leave. Now.»}

{230}{}{«How do we change Cesareo's mind?»}
{231}{}{«He has to see that surviving here is impossible. Otherwise... someone might slip scorpion venom into his food.»}
{232}{}{«Yeah. That won't be easy.»}
{233}{}{«Still... the poison idea has potential.»}
{234}{}{«He asked me to repair the lighthouse.»}
{235}{}{«Better to wreck the lighthouse machinery so it can never be lit.»}
{236}{}{«He asked me to look into rumors about monsters along the coast.»}
{237}{}{«He asked me to deal with the giant leeches.»}
{238}{}{«There you go. Proof this place isn't safe.»}
{239}{}{«He asked me to scout the surrounding area.»}
{240}{}{«Then lie to him. Tell him there's nothing here worth staying alive for.»}
